# infra-utm-anon-egress secrets.
#
# Copy to .env, or run `make preflight`. It creates .env from this file with
# generated passwords at mode 0600. .env is gitignored. Everything here is
# OPTIONAL: unset means "do not configure that feature", never a broken build.
# Secrets reach Ansible through a 0600 vars file, never `-e key=value`, which
# would be visible to every user in `ps auxww`.
#
# What does NOT belong here, or anywhere on disk: your MULLVAD ACCOUNT NUMBER.
# Nothing in this build needs it, the WireGuard configs carry their own keys.
# It is a bearer credential that cannot be rotated, so keep it out of your
# shell history, your scrollback and anything that keeps a transcript. If it
# has ever been exposed, buy a new account; and note that deleting a local
# config does not revoke a WireGuard key, you must remove it at Mullvad.

# --- Console passwords ------------------------------------------------------
# Console/GUI only; SSH stays key-only on both VMs. cloud-init locks the
# account, so without these the console shows boot output but accepts no login.
# For the WORKSTATION that is the difference between having a recovery path and
# not: it has no host port forward, so if the gateway or its sshd fails, the UTM
# console is the only way in. The desktop greeter needs one too.
#
# Separate per VM: compartmentalisation is the point, and the gateway is the
# box holding the VPN credentials.
GATEWAY_CONSOLE_PASSWORD=""
WORKSTATION_CONSOLE_PASSWORD=""

# --- Exit selection ---------------------------------------------------------
# Acquire the Mullvad account anonymously: Monero or cash, never bank-linked.
# The config is installed on the GATEWAY only.
#
# MULLVAD_EXIT is the country the internet sees, at any precision: "bg",
# "bg-sof", or "bg-sof-wg-001". One config per server must sit in secrets/ as
# <hostname>.conf. Leave it empty and the gateway simply has no tunnel yet,
# so you always have to set this one.
MULLVAD_EXIT=""

# The server the gateway connects to; same notation. Empty means any active
# server in a country OTHER than the exit's, which is the point of the second
# hop: the entry sees your IP but not your destination, the exit the reverse.
# Personally I select "se" here for Sweden, where all servers are owned by
# Mullvad, but you can decide whatever, since all servers are RAM only anyway.
MULLVAD_ENTRY=""

# The pair is pinned in generated/ so `make configure` cannot move your tunnel
# mid-lab. `make destroy` clears it; editing MULLVAD_EXIT discards it.
